+## Buying a condo or HOA home: will the seller's unpaid dues follow you?
+In a condo, only up to what the association puts in writing. A condo buyer is liable with the seller for unpaid dues, but only up to the amount in the statement the association must issue on request. The unpaid dues are paid from the sale price at closing, after taxes and recorded mortgages. That limit does not cover a buyer at a foreclosure sale.
