-<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I put my house on the MLS without an agent?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only through a broker, since the MLS is the database real estate brokers share. In NAR's 2025 survey, 7 percent of sellers who used an agent said the agent put the home on the MLS and did little else."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to tell a buyer that someone died in the house?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. South Carolina does not require it. The same goes for the sex offender registry, and an illness highly unlikely to spread by living in the home. If a buyer asks you directly, you may not lie."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I sell my house as is in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. \"As is\" means without repairs. An as-is sale still needs the state's disclosure form, unless it is a sale that needs none, such as some family sales."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I pay tax when I sell my house by owner?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often not. Under federal tax law, you can leave up to $250,000 of gain out of your income, or $500,000 for a married couple filing jointly. You must have owned and lived in the home at least 2 of the last 5 years."}}]}</script>
+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Who pays the deed stamps when you sell by owner in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The seller pays them, whether or not an agent is involved: $1,295 on a $350,000 sale."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I sell my house to my son or daughter without the disclosure form?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, if the sale is only to your children, grandchildren, parents or grandparents. If your child's spouse is also a buyer, the sale needs the form."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to tell a buyer that someone died in the house?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. South Carolina does not require it. If a buyer asks you directly, you may not lie about it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I sell my house as is in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. An as-is sale still needs the state's disclosure form, unless it is one of the sales that need no form, such as some family sales."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a buyer use their own agent to buy a for-sale-by-owner home?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The buyer's written agreement with their agent says how that agent is paid. You can offer to pay that agent, or offer the buyer a credit toward their costs."}}]}</script>
